WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.850
One of the most poorly titled movies of all
time, The First Purge, invalidated 5 years

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.010
of me referring to THIS movie as the first
Purge. However, unlike the original Purge,

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.880
this one came out relatively close to when
the story takes place. The movie is set in

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.340
2016 and if you want to see me explain the
timeline watch this video.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.590
But being set closer to the release date affords
this movie an interesting opportunity to incorporate

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.789
current events for the first time. Like how
Isaiah has a poster for another poorly titled

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:29.190
movie: Halloween 2018 in his room. This is
part advertising for Blumhouse who wanted

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.809
to hype up their other big release for that
year, and part foreshadowing, as Isaiah and

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:36.100
his loved ones would hide in a closet at the
end of the movie, just like Laurie Strode

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.210
did in Halloween.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:41.069
To learn about the other references and hidden
meanings in The First Purge, stick around

00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:44.620
to the end of this video.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:50.800
There aren’t really any decent masks for
sale for The First Purge for whatever reason,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.309
so I’m gonna go bare for this one. Welcome to Things You
Missed. The initial three Purge films were

00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:59.309
both written and directed by James Demonaco,
but for this prequel, he’d stay on as screenwriter

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:02.159
while tasking Gerard McMurray with directing
duties.

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:05.580
Subtle is probably not the word best used
to describe any Purge film, but you could

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.380
at least make the argument that the themes
are subtle in 1 through 3, especially if you’ve

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.970
seen my videos analysing them. McMurray decided
to take a more direct approach.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.960
The poster for this movie and the line said
during this one scene are very obvious jabs

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.750
at the United States White House administration
during the time the movie was made, whereas

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.189
the previous movies depicted the NFFA as an
alternative to real life political parties.

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:27.970
As you know, we’re not here to talk about
the most obvious details in this movie, we’re

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.750
here to talk about the Things You Missed.
So let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.715
Here’s the Things You Missed screen.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.320
One detail I found interesting was how the
NFFA Chief of Staff intentionally sends his

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.140
mercenaries to purge in low-income areas.
This makes it appear as if the lower class

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.740
is out for blood, which almost directly leads
into the beginning of the original movie,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.421
where a group of affluent purgers hunt down
an innocent homeless man for no other reason

00:01:54.421 --> 00:01:55.990
than the fact that he is homeless.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.610
We’ve also seen that the NFFA likes to use
statistics to make it seem like The Purge

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.359
is helping reduce crime during the rest of
the year. Unfortunately, the NFFA website,

00:02:03.359 --> 00:02:07.249
which was updated with statistics and additional
lore to promote Purge movie releases in the

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:11.580
past has its weakest iteration for The First
Purge -- there’s basically no new information

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.080
here.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.250
But perhaps more importantly, at the beginning
of the movie, we see how this data was skewed.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.440
The scene suggests they are doing their research
about crime behaviour using crazies and addicts,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.780
as opposed to the general population. This
is a tactic they use to craft their own narrative.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.280
They want to make it seem The Purge is the
answer for the nation’s problems, but many

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.340
of their opposers see through the BS and protest
at the sign up stations, where citizens can

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.360
volunteer to participate in The Purge Experiment
in exchange for financial compensation. The

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.530
conflict draws in many news stations, including
one called KRXJ News, a station that has also

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.824
appeared in the TV show Psyche and in the
Marvel Cinematic Universe. 

00:02:44.824 --> 00:02:47.076
It seems it's appeared in a couple of other shows as well.

00:02:47.076 --> 00:02:47.970
Is this a coincidence?

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:48.970
I don’t think so.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:54.060
There are about 35,000 possible combinations
that start with either K or W. I tried Googling

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.810
a number of random combinations, and surprisingly,
they all seem to be taken. But KRXJ was the

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.500
only one I found that yielded a fictional
entity. 

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.230
After doing a little digging, I realized that
prop designer Daniel Columbie has also designed

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:10.140
for a few Marvel movies. I’m guessing that’s
the connection, and the answer to this pointless

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:10.662
question.

00:03:10.662 --> 00:03:14.837
The sign up stations also give away blue flowers
to those who sign up to participate.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:22.560
“Baptisias. The official flower of the experiment.
They represent rebirth.”

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.730
This explains the origin of a through line
in each of the Purge movies: the baptisias, which

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.510
became a sign of support for the Purge.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.150
STRANGER: “And your blue flowers tell me
that you support The Purge.”

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.840
The main antagonist this time is the original
NFFA Chief of Staff, Arlo Sabian. If you’ve

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.150
seen my other Purge episodes, you know that
Sabian is a name that comes up in every Purge

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.340
movie, which is perhaps just a symptom of
the fact that they are all written by James

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.670
Demonaco, who likes to have a character named
Sabian in all of his work.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.400
The other James Demonaco trademark is Staten
Island, where the Purge experiment is going

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.120
to take place. This location appears on a
TV screen in preceding Purge movies,

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.200
and the two non-Purge movies he’s directed
are both set there.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.980
But not far from where this is taking place, our
main character, Nya, leads a protest against

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:04.171
the controversial experiment. One of the signs
reads “The 28th is a h*te crime”. This

00:04:04.171 --> 00:04:08.550
suggests that The Purge is being considered
as the 28th Amendment to the US Constitution,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.760
which is confirmed in the original iteration
of the website.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:15.280
But I think this movie creates an interesting
metaphor for The Constitution. Nya and Isaiah

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.390
live at a building called The Park Towers.
Let’s pretend that building is The US Constitution.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:23.560
It’s an old building. It has a lot of leaks
that have come up over the years. The people

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.850
that live there have a lot of issues with
it. The problem is, the manager is never in,

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.220
and isn’t much help anyway with fixing these
issues anyways.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.240
Our characters are minorities, and they live
on the 14th floor. It just so happens that

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.720
the 14th Amendment deals with equal protection
of the laws, and is often used to fight racial

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:39.720
discrimination.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.560
This is fitting, because the NFFA hires modern
factions of racist groups such as the KKK

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.740
and Aryan Nations to go into Staten Island
and purge. The main bad guy, whose name is…

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:54.440
General Smiley?.. Has a gold armband very
similar to the red Nazi armband you might

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.290
see in generals wearing in old photographs.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:05:00.780
They attack the entire building floor by floor.
On the second floor, a couple of armed citizens

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.470
fight back against them. As it turns out,
the second amendment is the right to bear

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.160
arms, something citizens are reminded of in
the form of a huge billboard. The text at

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.420
the bottom says “Paid for by the UARO Political
Victory Fund. I have no idea what the UARO

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.870
is, but if you look up “political victory
fund” you’ll find a bunch of stuff about

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.720
the NRA, who are stated at the beginning of
the movie to be supporting the New Founding

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.720
Fathers.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:27.150
“The New Founding Fathers, rising in polls,
with the NRA now endorsing them and supporting

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:31.090
them financially with large donations to the
NFFA warchest.”

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.710
The implication is that The Purge is fueled
by money, that this whole thing happened because

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.320
the NFFA values money, more than it values
the lives of its citizens.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:44.849
“They have monetized and incentivized murder.
Walk away from their money!”

00:05:44.849 --> 00:05:48.930
The police officers who are keeping an eye
on this protest don’t seem too enthused,

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:54.543
but names like “Forbes” and “Sachs”,
maybe it’s because they are in on it as well.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.800
Staten Island was chosen as the site of the
experiment partially because it is home to

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.790
a number of street gangs, one of which is
led by a man named Dmitri who surprisingly

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:14.710
operates out of a community center named after
Jamaican activist Marcus Garvey.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.110
You’ve probably noticed that this movie
picks up where Election Year left off comparing

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:22.860
the anti-Purge movement to the American Civil
Rights movement. The First Purge is, as usual,

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:26.550
a lot less subtle about it; there’s one
point where Nya even claims that she sees

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:30.580
The Purge as a way the government is trying
to keep minorities down. In Election Year,

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.230
Joe’s Deli was the center of the community,
and it displayed the photos of several Civil

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.230
Rights leaders.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:38.880
In The First Purge, the community center has
some of these same photos. Literally, we see

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:44.260
the same exact picture for Martin Luther King
Jr and a very similar picture for Malcolm X. I don’t know if this was

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.570
the production just trying to save a few bucks
on props, but it actually makes me wonder

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:51.430
if Joe from Election Year might have been
a youngster at this very community center,

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.210
and took these photos with him when he went
to DC to start the deli.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.620
We know he has been a part of gang activity
before.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.380
“Told you I ain’t no saint. Everybody’s
got a past.”

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:05.270
The other photos include civil rights figures:
Jesse Jackson, Marcus Garvey, Thurgood Marshall;

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.860
and the corkboard celebrates athletes who
broke the color barrier, like Jesse Owens,

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.830
Mohammed Ali and Jackie Robinson. Robinson
came up with the Brooklyn Dodgers playing

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.630
first base, but faced a lot of adversity because
he was the first African American-American

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:21.260
to play in MLB, as opposed to the Negro Leagues.
Brooklyn is right next to Staten Island, and

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.919
there’s a scene later in the film where
a black man is purged by white police officers

00:07:24.919 --> 00:07:28.940
just in front of first base at a
stadium with advertisements for The Purge

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.901
experiment displayed in the outfield. So it
feels like the movie is telling us that The

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:36.780
Purge gave bad people the opportunity to undo
the progress made by people like Jackie Robinson.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.949
And while we’re talking about sports, I
have to say that there was a huge missed

00:07:39.949 --> 00:07:44.040
opportunity by the wardrobe department. They
gave this guy, Taz, an Eli Manning jersey.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:48.419
But they should have given him #17 for Plaxico
Burress, seeing as how Taz later gets shot

00:07:48.419 --> 00:07:52.350
in the leg, and Plaxico Burress infamously
shot himself in the leg at a nightclub.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:55.840
Gotta love the character of Dmitri though,
I mean how many powerful gangsters have time

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.550
to also be an inspiring community basketball
coach? When it comes to gangsters named Dmitri,

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.790
this guy is probably in my top 2 or 3.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:06.900
In Dmitri’s office, he has a giant artwork
of Ben Franklin, as seen on the 100 dollar

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.880
bill. In universe, the reason he has it simply
because he likes money, but there are many

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.430
shots where the eye peeks through, as if it
is watching and spying on him.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:18.100
Ben Franklin is one of America’s original
founding fathers, and in the film, the government

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.960
is controlled by a party called the New Founding
Fathers, and they are notorious for spying

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.560
on the citizens, whether it be through surveillance
cameras, recording contact lenses or attack

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:27.060
drones.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.340
Another symbol for this can be seen in the
party scene, where a giant eyeball is passed

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.350
around in the crowd.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.889
The party goers wear animal masks and makeup,
such as foxes, lions, leopards and cows. I

00:08:35.889 --> 00:08:39.449
think I spotted a wendigo in there too. This
is a way of foreshadowing the predator prey

00:08:39.449 --> 00:08:43.800
relationship between the NFFA and the public.
And speaking of masks, there’s a scene where

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.139
Nya is trapped by a guy with a creepy baby
doll mask. The repurposing of a baby doll

00:08:48.139 --> 00:08:52.529
seems to be a nod to the remote control camera
created by Charlie Sandin in the original

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:53.078
Purge.

00:08:53.078 --> 00:08:57.079
“Quit playing with Timmy and come help me
set the table, Kiddo”

00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:00.130
Since this is a prequel, there are some things
that we’ve come to know about the world

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.769
of The Purge that seemingly haven’t been
instituted yet. I noticed that the vehicles

00:09:03.769 --> 00:09:08.279
have New York license plates, where in later
entries, the NFFA have instituted a uniform

00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:11.420
license plate for the US that says “A Nation
Reborn.”

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:15.509
This was also before the US Postal Service
was replaced with NFFA Mail.

00:09:15.509 --> 00:09:18.740
Another difference is that the color of the
emergency broadcast screen was red instead

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.829
of the usual blue. Director Gerard McMurray
kind of flipped the script when it comes to

00:09:22.829 --> 00:09:26.529
color. Other than this one graphic at the
very end of Election Year, the NFFA is always

00:09:26.529 --> 00:09:31.119
associated with the color blue. Perhaps the
NFFA intentionally chose light blue so that

00:09:31.119 --> 00:09:35.249
the public associates them with the good guys.
Think about pop culture: good guys blue, bad

00:09:35.249 --> 00:09:36.249
guys red.

00:09:36.249 --> 00:09:40.699
But McMurray uses light in this movie to reveal
the true allegiances of characters. In addition

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:44.390
to the red emergency broadcast, there’s
the NFFA headquarters, the hunters that try

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.920
to purge Isaiah, and Sabian steps into the
red light after revealing the true sinister

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.509
intentions of the experiment.

00:09:50.509 --> 00:09:55.110
Isaiah has blue contacts, Nya’s church is
blue, and Dmitri’s car has a blue underglow.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:58.780
Dmitri’s office is also blue, but when the
assassins enter the room, they come from the

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.410
lone red light in the corner.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:04.491
The office also has a picture of a man in
red boxing against a man in blue; The Purge

00:10:04.491 --> 00:10:07.759
is like a punch in the face from the government
to those that oppose them.

00:10:07.759 --> 00:10:11.700
Interestingly, Skeletor is the only character
whose contact lenses are purple, a combination

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:16.170
of red and blue. The bystanders who stay home
are green, and the looters are usually green

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.240
and occasionally orange.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.209
It’s possible that there’s also a political
side to McMurray’s decision to color code.

00:10:21.209 --> 00:10:25.069
In the US, Green is representative of the
third party, so maybe that’s why green is

00:10:25.069 --> 00:10:27.279
used to portray those that seem to be neutral.

00:10:27.279 --> 00:10:31.420
The artwork in Dmitri’s office is also representative
of the differing ways that Nya and Dmitiri

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.970
deal with their problems. In one scene, Nya
confronts him because she was upset that her

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:38.639
younger brother was getting involved in his
operation. She criticizes him for what his

00:10:38.639 --> 00:10:42.190
gang has done to their community. As they
argue, Dmitri is standing in front of the

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:44.790
two boxers -- he solves his problems with
aggression.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:48.970
The artwork behind Nya also depicts a boxer,
but he is sitting in the dark, thinking and

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.899
quietly reflecting. Nya solves her issues
with her head.

00:10:51.899 --> 00:10:55.629
Isaiah had been hurt while selling illegal
substances on the street for Dmitri. Nya is

00:10:55.629 --> 00:10:59.259
vocally against him him doing this, and their
apartment is covered with signage that says

00:10:59.259 --> 00:11:03.060
“Drug Free Zone” and “No Smoking”.
Dimitri’s gangs rule the streets, but the

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.920
apartment acts as a safe haven for Isaiah.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:09.069
I also noticed that their building looks very
similar to the example of low-income housing

00:11:09.069 --> 00:11:14.180
that Dante Bishop shows on TV during Election
Year. Election Year takes place 24 years later,

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:18.780
so these images illustrate how nothing ever
actually improved while the NFFA was in power.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:22.370
Comparing the technology from The First Purge
to Election Year highlights one of the many

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:25.870
frustrating things about The Purge franchise
-- which is that technology actually seems

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:30.410
to get worse as time goes on. Election Year
has a lot of tech that feels old even today.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:34.269
The coolest gadget in the series is probably
The First Purge’s video contact lenses,

00:11:34.269 --> 00:11:37.829
which are actually based on a real concept
that Sony has filed patents for, but we are

00:11:37.829 --> 00:11:41.639
still years and years away from seeing in
practice as I record this video in 2021.

00:11:41.639 --> 00:11:45.670
Now I’m gonna get to the end of the movie,
and why it makes no sense, but before I do,

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:48.639
it’s that part of the video, where I’ve
gotta air them out a little bit. During the

00:11:48.639 --> 00:11:52.319
robbery at this cash for gold place, why does
the store owner only have a security shade

00:11:52.319 --> 00:11:56.420
over one window? And I like how he keeps his
neon signs on, so he can advertise to criminals

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.420
that he has valuables.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:01.670
Also, there’s no way Dmitri would have survived
this crash, but he’s perfectly fine a couple

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:02.670
minutes later?

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:06.140
One thing I did find interesting is that the
mercenaries that Sabian sent into the Purge

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:10.350
to give the appearance that people had participated
are hidden in everyday vehicles, like a plumber’s

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.160
truck and a veteran transport van.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:16.561
Now the ending of the movie is a bit unconventional.
With Dmitri’s help, Nya, Isaiah and the

00:12:16.561 --> 00:12:20.509
others are able to ward off General Smiley,
Skeletor and the rest of the bad guys, and

00:12:20.509 --> 00:12:21.839
The Purge ends.

00:12:21.839 --> 00:12:25.929
Usually at the end of the movie, you see that
the character has changed somehow. We call it: character

00:12:25.929 --> 00:12:29.279
arc. But when Nya asks Dmitri what’s next
he tells her:

00:12:29.279 --> 00:12:31.970
“Now we fight.”

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:35.709
Which kind of goes against the message of
the movie, which has shown us how fighting

00:12:35.709 --> 00:12:39.889
basically nearly destroyed the community.
So it’s kind of like a “bad guys win anyway”

00:12:39.889 --> 00:12:43.089
scenario, because conflict is exactly what
the NFFA wants.

00:12:43.089 --> 00:12:46.660
This ending also might be suggesting that
Dmitri was kind of like the start of the resistance,

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:51.550
kind of a seed that would grow into the anti-NFFA
group that we meet later on in The Purge Anarchy,

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:53.639
as more people in different cities get involved.

00:12:53.639 --> 00:12:57.410
That group is probably not the most notable
resistance in the Purge franchise though,

00:12:57.410 --> 00:13:01.279
I would give that honor to the group we see
in another poorly titled installment, The

00:13:01.279 --> 00:13:05.610
